#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Manage files across runs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore libmagic */}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Manage files across runs {#manage-files-across-runs}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* <Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Placeholder content\">\n"
"- **File storage path.** `/function_user_data` is the path where the Fleets runner mounts file storage. Confirm that it is a supported path before publishing.\n"
"- **Supported file types.** The list of accepted and rejected types comes from the upload check in the gateway. Confirm the list, and whether CSV files will be accepted, before publishing.\n"
"- **Maximum file size.** Confirm the maximum file size (possibly 50 MB) before publishing.\n"
"</Admonition> */}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A managed workflow job works like a batch job on an HPC compute node. The "
"job's local disk is scratch space. The job can write to it, but the workflow"
" deletes it when the job ends. To keep files after the job ends, save them "
"to file storage, which works like your own storage bucket. Files that you "
"upload, and files that your workflow saves, remain in file storage, and "
"later runs of the workflow can read them.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each workflow has its own file storage for each user. Other users who run "
"the same workflow do not see your files.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![File storage for the workflow sits at the center. Your local notebook "
"reaches it with the client file methods file_upload(), files(), "
"file_download(), and file_delete(). File storage is yours only, because "
"other users of the workflow do not see your files. It is kept after each job"
" ends and is shared by all of your runs, and a file with the same name "
"replaces the earlier file. Each job sees file storage as the folder "
"/function_user_data. Run 1 also has a local disk at /tmp, which is deleted "
"when the job ends, and copies finished files from /tmp to "
"/function_user_data. Run 2 reads the files that earlier runs "
"saved.](/docs/images/managed-workflows/manage-files.svg)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Upload an input file {#upload-an-input-file}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Upload a file from your local notebook with `file_upload()`, and then list "
"the files in storage with `files()`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* REVIEW: the gateway sets no size limit for uploaded files "
"(gateway/main/settings.py, specs/ARGUMENTS_LIMIT.md). The Helm ingress sets "
"proxy-body-size to 50m. Confirm the limit in production. */}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Supported file types {#supported-file-types}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A managed workflow checks the contents of each uploaded file, not its "
"extension, and rejects files of other types:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Accepted | Rejected |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| JSON, plain text, YAML, and Python files; binary files such as NumPy (`.npy`, `.npz`), QPY, and pickle files; tar, gzip, and zip archives | CSV, PNG, PDF, HDF5, and empty files |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* REVIEW: let's figure out if this is recent, and what the file size "
"limitation actually is (50 MB?) */}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "File names {#file-names}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Use only letters, digits, underscores (`_`), hyphens (`-`), and periods "
"(`.`).** A managed workflow removes other characters, such as spaces, from "
"the name when you download or delete a file. For example, you can upload `my"
" results.json`, but you cannot download it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**File storage has no folders.** `file_upload()` keeps only the file name, "
"so `inputs/params.json` is stored as `params.json`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* REVIEW: upload does not sanitize file names, but download and delete do "
"(gateway/api/utils.py sanitize_file_name()). Confirm whether upload should "
"reject or sanitize these names. */}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Read files in a workflow {#read-files-in-a-workflow}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Pass the name of the file when you run the workflow:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To enable this, edit your workflow code to read the file from "
"`/function_user_data`, which is where every job sees file storage:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Inside a job, read and write files through this folder. The client file "
"methods, such as `file_upload()` and `file_download()`, are for your local "
"notebook.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "To read an archive, extract it to the local disk:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Write temporary files to `/tmp`. File storage is object storage that the job"
" sees as a folder, so file storage is slower than the local disk. Do heavy "
"reads and writes on the local disk, and copy finished files to file "
"storage.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* REVIEW: confirm how the mount behaves for appends, renames, and partial "
"writes, and how soon a file that one job writes is visible to a job that is "
"running at the same time. */}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Save output files {#save-output-files}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Your local notebook reads the names of the output files from the result:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To enable this, save each output file at the top level of "
"`/function_user_data`, and return the file names with `save_result()`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Files that the job writes outside `/function_user_data`, such as in `/tmp` "
"or the current folder, are deleted when the job ends.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* REVIEW: confirm that the mount stores "
"/function_user_data/<folder>/<file> as the storage key "
".../data/<folder>/<file>, so that later jobs can read subfolders. "
"file_download() can't fetch these files: sanitize_file_name() strips \"/\", "
"and files() lists only the base name (file_storage_fleets.py "
"get_public_files()). */}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Download output files {#download-output-files}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After the job ends, download each file with `file_download()`. Set "
"`target_name` to choose the local file name, and `download_location` to "
"choose an existing local folder:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Without `target_name`, `file_download()` adds a random prefix to the local "
"file name, such as `downloaded_3f2a9c1b_energies.npy`, and returns the name "
"that it used.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Download many outputs as one archive {#download-many-outputs-as-one-archive}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If a job saves many output files, or files in subfolders, bundle them into "
"one archive in the workflow, and download only the archive:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To enable this, write the outputs to a folder on the local disk, add the "
"folder to an archive in `/tmp`, and copy the archive to file storage:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because the archive is built on the local disk and copied in one step, file "
"storage never holds an incomplete archive. The archive keeps the folder "
"structure, and it can contain files of any type. In this example, the files "
"are extracted to `outputs/<run_name>/`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Delete files {#delete-files}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A managed workflow does not delete files from file storage, so files remain "
"until you delete them with `file_delete()`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`file_delete()` reports success even if the file does not exist, so check "
"the name with `files()` first. To delete all the files of one run, filter "
"`files()` by the run's name prefix, as described in the next section:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* REVIEW: on Fleets, deleting a missing file returns \"Requested file was "
"deleted.\" because gateway/core/ibm_cloud/cos/cos_client.py delete_object() "
"treats a missing key as deleted. Confirm whether file_delete() should return"
" 404 instead. */}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Best practice: give each run's files a unique name {#best-practice-give-"
"each-runs-files-a-unique-name}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"All of your runs of a workflow share the same file storage, and a file that "
"a job saves replaces any stored file with the same name. If you start "
"several runs at the same time and each run saves `energies.npy`, only the "
"last one is kept.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As a best practice, pass a run name as an argument, and start the name of "
"every file that the run saves with it:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"All runs can read the same input file, `hamiltonian.npz`, because they only "
"read it. Upload a shared input one time, before you start the runs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use run names that you can recognize later, and that contain only letters, "
"digits, underscores, hyphens, and periods. With one prefix for each run, you"
" can find, download, and [delete](#delete-files) the files of a run "
"together.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Best practice: checkpoint long jobs {#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A job that is canceled, fails, or reaches the 24-hour limit loses everything"
" that is not in file storage. For long runs, save a checkpoint to file "
"storage at regular intervals, and resume from it when you run the workflow "
"again with the same run name:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To continue a run that stopped, call `run()` again with the same "
"arguments.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Keep the following points in mind:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Write the checkpoint to the local disk first, and then copy it.** If the "
"job stops during a write, the stored checkpoint is incomplete, and the next "
"run cannot read it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Choose an interval that matches the cost of a step.** Save often enough "
"that you do not lose much work, but not so often that writing checkpoints "
"slows the job.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Delete checkpoints after the run succeeds.** A later run with the same "
"name then starts from the beginning.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a job that is canceled, you can also save partial results in a "
"[`SIGTERM` handler](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-"
"a-job-is-canceled).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- [Run a parameter sweep](/guides/run-parameter-sweep) to start one job for each input.\n"
"- [Write logs and handle errors](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors) to save partial results when a job is canceled.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
